{"id":"7d6da4bef6932415","group":"58","path":"58/batch03/58-thm-absoluteness-calculation.md","title":"Absoluteness Calculation","display":"thm-absoluteness-calculation — Absoluteness Calculation","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-absoluteness-calculation","aliases":["58-thm-absoluteness-calculation","Absoluteness Calculation","Absoluteness of Operations"],"display":"thm-absoluteness-calculation — Absoluteness Calculation","depends_on":["[[../batch17/58-df-formula.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-zfc-delta-zero-formula.md]]","[[../batch07/58-df-free-variable.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","[[../batch13/58-df-transitive.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-absoluteness-calculation"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-absoluteness-calculation</span><span>Absoluteness Calculation</span><span>Absoluteness of Operations</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-absoluteness-calculation — Absoluteness Calculation"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"65418b505fc53093\" href=\"?note=65418b505fc53093\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-formula.md\">../batch17/58-df-formula.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"2678ecfefaa83e32\" href=\"?note=2678ecfefaa83e32\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-zfc-delta-zero-formula.md\">../batch16/58-df-zfc-delta-zero-formula.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"715a32e91161b34f\" href=\"?note=715a32e91161b34f\" title=\"../batch07/58-df-free-variable.md\">../batch07/58-df-free-variable.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"2d9fd66bae7ead5a\" href=\"?note=2d9fd66bae7ead5a\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-transitive.md\">../batch13/58-df-transitive.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M,\\varphi,s\\in V\">\\(M,\\varphi,s\\in V\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M\\neq\\varnothing\">\\(M\\neq\\varnothing\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal L_\\in\">\\(\\mathcal L_\\in\\)</span> is the pure membership language</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Transitive}:V\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{Transitive}:V\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{DeltaZeroFormula}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{DeltaZeroFormula}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{FV}_{\\mathcal L_\\in}:V\\to V\">\\(\\operatorname{FV}_{\\mathcal L_\\in}:V\\to V\\)</span> are the parameter-coding interfaces</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{AbsoluteToV}_{\\mathrm{meta}}\">\\(\\mathrm{AbsoluteToV}_{\\mathrm{meta}}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\models_{\\mathrm{meta}}\">\\(\\models_{\\mathrm{meta}}\\)</span> are the metatheoretic predicate and truth notation defined below</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}absolute\\text{-}to\\text{-}V}\\vdash_{\\mathrm{meta}}\n\\mathrm{AbsoluteToV}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(\\varphi,M)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\leftrightarrow\nM\\neq\\varnothing\\land\\mathrm{Transitive}(M)\n\\land\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\mathcal L_\\in)\n\\land\\forall s\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Function}(s,\\operatorname{FV}_{\\mathcal L_\\in}(\\varphi),M)\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{9em}\\to\\bigl(\n\\langle M,\\in\\cap M^2\\rangle\\models_{\\mathrm{meta}}\\varphi[s]\n\\leftrightarrow V\\models_{\\mathrm{meta}}\\varphi[s]\\bigr)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}absolute\\text{-}to\\text{-}V}\\vdash_{\\mathrm{meta}}\n\\mathrm{AbsoluteToV}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(\\varphi,M)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\leftrightarrow\nM\\neq\\varnothing\\land\\mathrm{Transitive}(M)\n\\land\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\mathcal L_\\in)\n\\land\\forall s\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Function}(s,\\operatorname{FV}_{\\mathcal L_\\in}(\\varphi),M)\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{9em}\\to\\bigl(\n\\langle M,\\in\\cap M^2\\rangle\\models_{\\mathrm{meta}}\\varphi[s]\n\\leftrightarrow V\\models_{\\mathrm{meta}}\\varphi[s]\\bigr)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}absoluteness\\text{-}calculation}\\vdash_{\\mathrm{meta}}\nM\\neq\\emptyset\\land\\mathrm{Transitive}(M)\n\\land\\mathrm{DeltaZeroFormula}_S(\\varphi,\\mathcal L_\\in)\n\\to\\mathrm{AbsoluteToV}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(\\varphi,M).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}absoluteness\\text{-}calculation}\\vdash_{\\mathrm{meta}}\nM\\neq\\emptyset\\land\\mathrm{Transitive}(M)\n\\land\\mathrm{DeltaZeroFormula}_S(\\varphi,\\mathcal L_\\in)\n\\to\\mathrm{AbsoluteToV}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(\\varphi,M).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Bounded quantifiers range over elements of parameters already in <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M\">\\(M\\)</span>; transitivity makes those ranges identical in <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M\">\\(M\\)</span> and in <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"V\">\\(V\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>No assumption that <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M\">\\(M\\)</span> satisfies all of ZF is needed for bounded-formula absoluteness.</li>\n<li>Full power-set formation is not absolute in general.</li>\n<li>Because one side is the proper class <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"V\">\\(V\\)</span>, this result is necessarily a metatheoretic schema.  The set-to-set predicate from the absoluteness definition is not called with <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"V\">\\(V\\)</span> as though it were a set argument.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch17/58-df-formula.md","status":"resolved","id":"65418b505fc53093","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch17/58-df-formula.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-zfc-delta-zero-formula.md","status":"resolved","id":"2678ecfefaa83e32","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-zfc-delta-zero-formula.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch07/58-df-free-variable.md","status":"resolved","id":"715a32e91161b34f","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch07/58-df-free-variable.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch13/58-df-transitive.md","status":"resolved","id":"2d9fd66bae7ead5a","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch13/58-df-transitive.md]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"M,\\varphi,s\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"M\\n